WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.947
Data types matter because Pandas uses them to decide what operations are possible.

00:00:05.947 --> 00:00:11.782
A number stored as text cannot be summarized correctly until we convert it.

00:00:11.782 --> 00:00:20.017
A date stored as a string cannot support reliable date operations until it becomes a datetime value.

00:00:20.017 --> 00:00:26.647
In the example, we use to numeric and to datetime with errors set to coerce.

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:34.007
Coerce means that invalid values are converted to missing values instead of causing the program to stop.

00:00:34.007 --> 00:00:38.627
This is useful because conversion becomes part of the quality audit.

00:00:38.627 --> 00:00:47.112
The invalid date becomes visible as a missing datetime value, and a missing or malformed amount becomes a missing

00:00:47.112 --> 00:00:52.927
numeric value. Run the code and compare the values and data types before and after conversion.

00:00:52.927 --> 00:00:57.072
Remember that conversion does not automatically solve the problem.

00:00:57.072 --> 00:01:01.079
It helps us identify which values need further investigation.
